course: dictionary
lesson: 5909
title: A word for sailors
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mariner is a sailor, a person who works on a ship. You may meet it in old stories and poems, where it sounds grand and a little old-fashioned. «The Mariner sits on his raft trailing his toes in the water» tells you he is out on the sea.
explain: Context helps you here. Raft, water and the sea are clues that the mariner works on the water. Try swapping in sailor: «The sailor sits on his raft trailing his toes in the water» still makes sense, so sailor is the right meaning.
explain: In «The Rime of the Ancient Mariner», a poem by Samuel Taylor Coleridge, a mariner is a sailor who shot a bird called an albatross. The word can also sound grand, as in «a man of infinite-resource-and-sagacity», which means endlessly clever and full of good sense.
fact: Mariner means a sailor, a person who works on a ship.
fact: Mariners in history used compasses and the stars to find their way across the sea.
fact: Phrases you may meet are the Ancient Mariner, master mariner (a very skilled sea captain) and mariner's compass.
fact: With a capital M, Mariner can be a name, such as NASA's Mariner probes or the Seattle Mariners baseball team.
fact: The plural is mariners, which means more than one sailor.
exercise: «The Mariner sits on his raft trailing his toes in the water.» Who is the Mariner? | A whale that swims in the sea | A railway guard calling out the stations | A pebble beach | *A sailor, a person who works on a ship
exercise: Mariners in history used the stars and a compass to find their way. What does mariners mean? | Birds that fly over the sea | *Sailors | Fish that swim in the sea | People who build railway stations
exercise: Find and copy one word from this list that means a sailor. | ship | *mariner | raft | sea
test: Coleridge's poem «The Rime of the Ancient Mariner» tells of a sailor who shot a bird. What is the sailor called in the title? | *Mariner | Albatross | Coleridge | Rime
test: What does a mariner's compass help a sailor do? | *Find the right direction at sea | Ride a horse across the hills | Cook a fish dinner | Paint a picture of the waves
exam: The sailor is «a man of infinite-resource-and-sagacity», so he is clever and full of good sense. What is a mariner? | A clever bird that sings | A type of whale | *A sailor, a person who works on a ship | A tall mountain by the sea
